WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.167
The final SELECT exposes the results of the pipeline.

00:00:03.167 --> 00:00:07.367
Phone candidates are only kept when they satisfy the ten-digit teaching rule.

00:00:07.367 --> 00:00:11.662
Unsupported dates remain NULL. Duplicate rank remains visible.

00:00:11.662 --> 00:00:16.332
The row status flags records that still contain important unresolved problems.

00:00:16.332 --> 00:00:21.882
This is what transparent cleaning looks like: useful output plus visible uncertainty.

00:00:21.882 --> 00:00:27.657
Connect this idea to a product catalog standardizing categories and quarantining invalid rows.

00:00:27.657 --> 00:00:32.587
Ask what could go wrong if the concept were misunderstood: could rows be duplicated,

00:00:32.587 --> 00:00:39.357
important records disappear, categories be interpreted incorrectly, or a report become difficult to reproduce?

00:00:39.357 --> 00:00:44.297
A strong analyst can explain both the SQL operation and the assumption behind it.

00:00:44.297 --> 00:00:49.435
After the example, summarize the idea in one plain-language sentence before moving on.
